{
  "title": "Glue-on SMA antenna bracket",
  "summary": "A small L-bracket glued to an enclosure that holds a rubber-duck antenna upright on its SMA bulkhead connector. Three per plate.",
  "status": "preview",
  "date": "2026-11-02",
  "material": "PLA (PETG if the box lives outdoors in the sun)",
  "notes": "Back plate 30 × 36 mm glued flat to the box (the bed side, textured by the PEI plate, takes glue well). A 3.5 mm shelf at the top reaches 24 mm out; the SMA bulkhead's thread goes up through its 6.6 mm hole (1/4\"-36 thread + clearance), nut and antenna on top, connector body and pigtail hanging underneath between two 45° gussets, so the antenna stands upright without using its hinge. The hole's centre is 15 mm from the wall, so the connector body and a spanner fit underneath. Prints on the glue face with no supports; the hole is a teardrop whose point (away from the wall) hides under the nut's washer. Glue: epoxy or thick superglue on a roughened, degreased box (sand the box lightly; polypropylene boxes hold glue badly, polycarbonate/ABS well). 30 % gyroid infill and 4 walls (functional part). 3 brackets, 0.16 mm layers, about 42 min and 22 g.",
